# .npmignore — defense-in-depth against private content shipping to npm.
#
# Note: package.json `files` is the primary whitelist; npm publishes the
# union of `files` minus this list. These patterns exist so that even if
# `files` accidentally widens to include a glob like `**/*.md`, no private
# data ships.
#
# Keep in sync with the leak patterns in .gitignore.

# Internal project state — never ship
.adhdev/
ADHDEV.md
CLAUDE.md

# Private docs and reports
docs/
audit-report.md
build-check.md

# Dev / build artifacts
*.bak
*.log
.env
.env.local
pending-mentions.json
.claude-preview/
.claude-tmp/
.tmp-tgz-audit/
adhdev-board-*.tgz
next-env.d.zip
Codebase 1.zip
.relates.txt
.tags.txt
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test scaffolding (the runtime doesn't need it)
tests/
vitest.config.*

# Source files (we ship the Next build output, not raw sources)
src/
